\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Feedback and task loss on the independent core. (a) Actual matched paths for seed 1002, $-30^\circ $, the first proportional 50\%-deletion collision in seed order; this is a descriptive example. Solid/dashed paths are agent/pursuer, truncated at first contact; the dotted circle has 50-mm contact radius. (b) All 288 outcomes: 24 seed rows, two laws, three network conditions and two bearings. Column totals are successes out of 24; within-seed cells are paired. (c) Registered relay-minus-proportional net-loss contrasts with 95\% whole-seed bootstrap intervals and Holm-adjusted $p$. Equal healthy success does not match safety reserve or turning effort.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v9-outcomes}{{2}{4}{}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Frozen precontact warnings versus task outcome. (a) Every 100--400-ms command-rate observation, with visual vertical jitter and the healthy-validation cutoff. Most later collisions retain command transmission. (b) Detection among 13 collisions versus false alarms among 275 successes; intervals are 95\% whole-seed bootstrap ranges. Geometric forecasts use exact simulated state. Zero observed misses are not zero risk. Complete confusion counts remain in the supplement; these are scores of our records, not executions of SpikeFI or SpikingJET.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:v9-warnings}{{3}{4}{}{figure.3}{}}
